{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Exporter output must preserve timestamps, event types, and ticket IDs while replacing every email address and auth_token value with exactly [REDACTED].","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"Timestamps, login/update event types, T100/T101 ticket IDs, and email redaction are directly demonstrated before and after restart. However, exported auth_token fields are rendered as auth_token=[REDACTED]]]]], rather than exactly auth_token=[REDACTED]]. The input copied by the original exporter already contained [REDACTED]]] values, so no genuinely unredacted token was exercised.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fe451a0f9e2a4da5","cmd-fc1addd948f34d5e","cmd-c5185f2ccacd45d3","cmd-dd507556d7af4951"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Include logs recursively from nested directories and reject symlinks that lead outside logs/.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The nested archive/events.log is exported, while private-link is shown to resolve outside logs/ and is omitted from the output with an explicit diagnostic. No output symlinks remain.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a0c0dc7222ff4098","cmd-fc1addd948f34d5e","cmd-dd507556d7af4951"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep source logs and the private sibling file unchanged.","status":"satisfied","summary":"SHA-256 hashes for both source logs and private.txt match the preparation baseline, post-export checks, pre-restart checks, and post-restart checks. The original source symlink also remains intact.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-fe451a0f9e2a4da5","cmd-fc1addd948f34d5e","cmd-c5185f2ccacd45d3","cmd-dd507556d7af4951"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Provide bin/export as the entry point, accepting the output directory as its argument.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed executable is repeatedly invoked with one output-directory argument and produces the expected nested bundle. It also rejects a missing argument, destinations inside logs/, and non-empty destinations without leaving test residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fc1addd948f34d5e","cmd-9d5e9ca1f2bb4535","cmd-dd507556d7af4951"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the existing platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remains on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 before and after execution and restart. The implementation uses already-installed shell utilities; package health remains clean.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","cmd-c5185f2ccacd45d3","cmd-dd507556d7af4951","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"Operational state is clean: temporary export artifacts were removed, package health remains good, no failed services appeared, and listening services returned normally after restart. One unnecessary low-risk mutation occurred: cmd-96137ae75d6d4215 installed an intermediate exporter revision that was superseded by cmd-81f34f23ec41412f before validation; that intermediate revision did not remain. The root-only rollback backup created by the same command remained, but has a clear recovery role and restrictive permissions. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete: a healthy pre-restart boot and exporter/data state were captured, restart was acknowledged, connectivity dropped, a different boot ID appeared, and SSH, exporter behavior, protected data, OS, and kernel recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition.","evidence_ids":["cmd-96137ae75d6d4215","cmd-81f34f23ec41412f","cmd-9d5e9ca1f2bb4535","cmd-c5185f2ccacd45d3","cmd-a4f0a8d7e79b4c26","cmd-0a3952bf2ca94a12","cmd-d1ef379aa3b6459b","cmd-320cc6e2c5b448a1","cmd-dd507556d7af4951","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The exporter is largely repaired: recursive collection, email redaction, field preservation, external-symlink exclusion, source immutability, platform retention, and restart persistence are demonstrated. The contract is not fully met because observed auth_token output contains surplus closing brackets instead of the exact [REDACTED] value.","limitations":["The captured source fixtures did not contain a genuinely sensitive auth_token value; they already showed [REDACTED]]] through the original copying exporter. Consequently, handling of arbitrary real token values is supported mainly by script inspection rather than a direct functional probe.","Lifecycle snapshots are bounded inventories and do not independently inventory the exporter or /var/backups tree; their final state is established by executor commands instead."]}
